   "source": [
    "When the built-in functions aren't enough, .apply() lets you pass any function to each group."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "38b879c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Basic Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5adb3abb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv\"\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(url)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c7f8a1e9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Range (max - min) of fares per class"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d8622994",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df.groupby(\"Pclass\")[\"Fare\"].apply(lambda x: x.max() - x.min())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8bb69f37",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Percentage of survivors in each class (custom calculation)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8121e18c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def survival_pct(group):\n",
    "    return group.sum() / group().count() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "df.groupby(\"Pclass\")[\"Survived\"].apply(survival_pct)"
   ]
  },
